# Panel 186 R7, lane land186, 2026-10-02: a group's record over a C union is
# built naming exactly one member of each union, so a construction may name
# fewer fields than the record declares, and `check` holds only its labels
# (`selfhost/check/group_fields.hero`); what it leaves out is `build`'s.
#
# A union TYPE built from two of its members is refused at the construction,
# naming the two. Until R7 it was told on the record's line, with a note that
# a record naming two members is never built, which R7 makes false: `UT`
# naming both is legal, and a construction names one.

extern "ffi-a-construction.h"
    record UT
        i: i32
        f: f32
    function ut_i(u: UT) -> i32

function main()
    u = UT(i: 1, f: 1.5)  #~ ffi_union_field
    print(ut_i(u))
